    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate with **Yordan Alvarez** anchoring the lineup as our definitive start (82.97). Facing Grayson Rodriguez, **Yordan Alvarez** benefits from an elite 0.474 xwOBA and a favorable matchup against a starter with a 5.28 xERA, making him the primary engine for our power categories. Joining him in the top tier are our speed-focused threats, **Caleb Durbin** (70.29) and **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (68.56). **Caleb Durbin** draws a soft matchup against Jacob Lopez, and we are aggressively deploying him to capitalize on a high-probability stolen base environment created by a slow delivery. Similarly, **Pete Crow-Armstrong** is a high-upside play at the top of the order; while Dustin May\u2019s hold rate presents a slight hurdle, the dynamic platoon advantage and leadoff positioning make him an essential asset in our pursuit of SB efficiency.\n\nOur most difficult roster decision today involved **Chase Meidroth**, who finished with a 32.85 efficiency score. He fell well below our 40.0 \"Zebras Floor,\" largely due to the difficult matchup against Cam Schlittler and a projected bottom-third lineup spot that severely capped his ceiling. Conversely, **Lars Nootbaar** (41.56) occupies the final outfield spot despite a weak score; he remains active only because we are monitoring his platoon splits, though he is on thin ice compared to the higher efficiency ratings provided by **Christian Yelich** (64.45) and **Carson Benge** (61.18). **Carson Benge** represents a high-reward start against Smith-Shawver, though managers should note a 45% rain risk in that stadium that could jeopardize his ability to accumulate full-game stats. We are also closely tracking the confirmed batting order for **Yordan Alvarez**, **Caleb Durbin**, **Lars Nootbaar**, and **Pete Crow-Armstrong** to ensure these projections hold, as any shift down the order would trigger an immediate re-evaluation of their efficiency scores.",
